rp2040: the SPI driver takes its DMA channels without waiting

Purpose: with CONFIG_RP2040_SPI_DMA, rp2040_spibus_initialize() takes the
port's two DMA channels with rp2040_dmachannel(), which waits for a free
channel for ever, and then uses the DMA for every exchange longer than
CONFIG_RP2040_SPI_DMATHRESHOLD words.  The board initializes SPI1 at the
NINA-W102's first request (common/drivers/nina/port/nuttx/
nina_bus_rp2040.c), in the requesting thread, after other users (the I2C0
DMA reads) have taken theirs; with fewer than two channels free that
request would wait for ever, where the port should go on polled.

- arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_spi.c: rp2040_spibus_initialize() takes the
  two channels with rp2040_dmachannel_trywait() (patch 0011: NULL at once
  when no channel is free).  Without both, the one it got is freed again,
  dmaenable stays false (every exchange polled, as without
  CONFIG_RP2040_SPI_DMA) and spierr() reports it.  The exchanges are
  unchanged.

Zephyr: the PL022 driver (drivers/spi/spi_pl022.c) requests its devicetree
channels with dma_request_channel() at boot, which does not wait either.

diff --git a/arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_spi.c b/arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_spi.c
index 5c10b99a..01a6d5cb 100644
--- a/arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_spi.c
+++ b/arch/arm/src/rp2040/rp2040_spi.c
@@ -827,17 +827,41 @@
   /* DMA settings */
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_RP2040_SPI_DMA
-  priv->txdmach = rp2040_dmachannel();
+  /* Take the two channels without waiting: without both, the port is
+   * polled.
+   */
+
+  priv->txdmach = rp2040_dmachannel_trywait();
   txconf.size = RP2040_DMA_SIZE_BYTE;
   txconf.noincr = false;
   priv->txconfig = txconf;
 
-  priv->rxdmach = rp2040_dmachannel();
+  priv->rxdmach = rp2040_dmachannel_trywait();
   rxconf.size = RP2040_DMA_SIZE_BYTE;
   rxconf.noincr = false;
   priv->rxconfig = rxconf;
 
-  priv->dmaenable = true;
+  if (priv->txdmach != NULL && priv->rxdmach != NULL)
+    {
+      priv->dmaenable = true;
+    }
+  else
+    {
+      if (priv->txdmach != NULL)
+        {
+          rp2040_dmafree(priv->txdmach);
+          priv->txdmach = NULL;
+        }
+
+      if (priv->rxdmach != NULL)
+        {
+          rp2040_dmafree(priv->rxdmach);
+          priv->rxdmach = NULL;
+        }
+
+      priv->dmaenable = false;
+      spierr("SPI%d: no DMA channels, polled\n", port);
+    }
 #endif
 
   /* Configure 8-bit SPI mode */
